# shir_nodes/element_read.node — ElementRead: index into an anonymous
# composite VALUE (`m["key"]` on a map literal, arr[i] on a literal,
# Java/Zig element reads on non-named collections).
#
# GENERIC. coll is any expression evaluating to a composite value; key
# stringifies like the host object model. Named-variable indexing keeps
# the existing A1 shapes (assocGet / arrayIndex / ${a[i]}) — THIS node
# covers only the expression-position form frontends previously had no
# shape for.

node ElementRead
tag "ElementRead"
kind expr
# storage_class str_bounded
field coll: expr
field key: expr
# Spec: TextOps#element_read_sound (docs/fm/TextOps/ShIR_TextOps_Strings.thy, section
# "ReadLine, ElementRead, FieldRead, TypeAssert: readback laws"). Reading one entry out
# of a composite VALUE lands on the MapLiteral association list: the read is
# `map_lookup` over the zipped entries with the query stringified by the abstract st.
# Proved: the read IS that lookup; reading a key that occurs LAST in a literal yields
# that last value (so a duplicate key reads back last-wins, exactly as the literal's own
# lookup does); and a literal none of whose keys stringify to the query has no such
# entry.
#
# NOT PROMISED (stated, not assumed): the stringification rule (abstract st, as for
# map_literal); the order of enumeration or property storage (JS reorders integer-like
# names); array INDEX arithmetic and out-of-range behaviour; the missing-key policy
# beyond "no such entry" (null vs undef vs an error is the host's).
spec: TextOps#element_read_sound
